<BaseLayout title="TCA · Cloud Accounting Software Analysis" description="Comparative analysis of cloud accounting software with public APIs for the TCA carve-out migration." initialHeaderDark={true}>

  <main class="aa-page">

    <div class="aa-header">
      <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--grey">Carve-Out · Finance Workstream</span>
      <h1 class="aa-title">
        Cloud Accounting Software &mdash; <em>API Analysis</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="aa-intro">
        The carve-out requires migrating TCA's accounting software by December. This analysis compares
        cloud accounting platforms for Italy on their <strong>public API catalogs</strong>, against two
        requirements &mdash; scoped to <strong>true general-ledger accounting</strong> (chart of accounts,
        double-entry, balances). Invoicing-only tools such as Fatture in Cloud do not qualify as the
        accounting backend.
      </p>
      <span class="deadline-badge">&#9679;&nbsp; Hard Deadline: December 2026</span>

      <div class="req-grid">
        <div class="req-card">
          <div class="req-label">Requirement 01 · Import (POST)</div>
          <p class="req-text">Push revenue data from the club's management system into the ledger, broken down by <strong>GL account</strong> and <strong>payment type/method</strong> (ideally also by revenue center).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="req-card">
          <div class="req-label">Requirement 02 · Extract (GET)</div>
          <p class="req-text">Pull consolidated data (account balances, trial balance, aggregated income/expenses) to feed <strong>dynamic external dashboards</strong> &mdash; Power BI, Looker Studio, custom apps.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <PhotoBand img="club-aerial.jpeg" eyebrow="One Ledger" line="Every euro — courts, bar, school — flowing into one ledger." />

    <!-- ── COMPARISON TABLE ── -->
    <h2 class="aa-section-title">01 · Comparison <em>Table</em></h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="aa-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Software</th>
            <th>True GL Accounting</th>
            <th>Public API</th>
            <th>POST Revenue<br />(account + payment)</th>
            <th>GET Balances /<br />Trial Balance</th>
            <th>Italian Compliance</th>
            <th>Regime 398/91<br />(ASD/SSD)</th>
            <th>Verdict</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {rows.map((r) => (
            <tr class={r.finalist ? 'row-finalist' : r.sports ? 'row-sports' : ''}>
              <td>{r.sw}{r.swNote && <div class="aa-note">{r.swNote}</div>}</td>
              <td>{r.gl}</td>
              <td>{r.api}</td>
              <td>{r.post}</td>
              <td>{r.get}</td>
              <td>{r.it}</td>
              <td>{r.regime398 ?? '—'}</td>
              <td>
                <span class={`aa-badge aa-badge--${r.vClass}`}>{r.verdict}</span>
                {r.vNote && <div class="aa-note">{r.vNote}</div>}
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <!-- ── FINALISTS ── -->
    <h2 class="aa-section-title">02 · The <em>Finalists</em></h2>
    <div class="fin-grid">
      <div class="fin-card fin-card--sport">
        <div class="fin-tag fin-tag--sport">Sports Specialist · Sector First Choice</div>
        <div class="fin-title">TeamSystem Sport (Sportivi in Cloud)</div>
        <p class="fin-text">The only option with <strong>native regime 398/91 support</strong> — the forfettario VAT mechanism, ASD/SSD rendiconto format, and member management are built in, not bolted on.</p>
        <ul class="fin-points">
          <li><strong>Regime 398/91:</strong> handles IVA forfettaria (1/3 of collected VAT on commercial income) natively; produces the <em>rendiconto economico-finanziario</em> required for non-commercial entities.</li>
          <li><strong>Membership:</strong> quote associative tracked as non-taxable; <em>compensi sportivi dilettantistici</em> managed within the IRPEF exemption thresholds.</li>
          <li><strong>Compliance 2024-2026:</strong> covers the mandatory e-invoicing obligation for ASD/SSD (since Jan 2024) and the 2026 shift from VAT exclusion to VAT exemption for sports activities.</li>
          <li><strong>Caveat:</strong> standalone public REST API less mature than Reviso or Odoo — verify dashboard integration depth before committing.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="fin-card">
        <div class="fin-tag">Finalist #1 · GL + API First Choice</div>
        <div class="fin-title">TeamSystem Contabilità in Cloud (ex Reviso)</div>
        <p class="fin-text">Italian-native cloud GL with a <strong>publicly documented REST API</strong> and a flat, predictable pricing model based on transaction volume — not per user. Best fit as the GL layer in a two-layer architecture (specialist club system + CiC for dashboards).</p>
        <ul class="fin-points">
          <li><strong>Pricing — per transaction volume, users unlimited:</strong> plans are sized by annual accounting entries. Entry plan: ~€25–29/mese (~6,000 entries/year); medium plan: ~€45–59/mese (~15,000 entries/year). All + IVA, billed annually. No per-user cost — the entire TCA team can access at the same price. <em>Note: confirm exact current figures at teamsystem.com/store/contabilita-in-cloud/prezzi.</em></li>
          <li><strong>Typical TCA cost:</strong> ~€45–59/mese → <strong>~€540–700/anno</strong> in licenze. Implementation: guided self-setup, no partner required (~€0–2,000 onboarding).</li>
          <li><strong>POST:</strong> journal entries and invoices via vouchers onto a real, customizable chart of accounts — revenue posted per GL account with the correct counterpart (cash, bank, POS) covers the payment-type breakdown.</li>
          <li><strong>GET:</strong> the <code>accounts</code> resource exposes <code>balance</code> per account plus entries by fiscal year/period — a trial balance via API, ready for Power BI / Looker Studio.</li>
          <li><strong>Italian compliance:</strong> native IVA, SDI/FatturaPA via TeamSystem ecosystem, export to studio commercialista, liquidazioni IVA.</li>
          <li><strong>Setup:</strong> fast — Italian product, no partner required, 14-day free trial, guided onboarding.</li>
          <li><strong>Regime 398/91:</strong> not native, requires manual COA configuration and accountant-side processes for forfettario VAT.</li>
          <li><strong>Ceiling:</strong> accounting only — no HR, no CRM, no member management, no multi-company, no ERP expansion path. If TCA grows beyond a single tennis club, this means switching systems.</li>
          <li><strong>Condition:</strong> confirm product roadmap with TeamSystem (the product is the rebranded Reviso) before signing.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="fin-card fin-card--caution">
        <div class="fin-tag fin-tag--caution">Finalist #2 · Conditional — but uniquely scalable</div>
        <div class="fin-title">Odoo Enterprise + Italian Localization</div>
        <p class="fin-text">The only option that starts as an accounting system and can grow into a <strong>full ERP — multi-module, multi-company, multi-country — without changing platform</strong>. If TCA's ambitions extend beyond a single tennis club entity, Odoo is the only finalist that keeps pace. The trade-off: higher Year 1 cost and a regime 398/91 gap that requires custom development.</p>
        <ul class="fin-points">
          <li><strong>Pricing — Custom plan, hosted by Odoo (SaaS):</strong> ~€34–42/utente/mese (Custom plan, billed annually; exact EUR via <a href="https://www.odoo.com/pricing-configurator" target="_blank" rel="noopener">odoo.com/pricing-configurator</a>). For 5 users: ~€170–210/mese → <strong>~€2,000–2,500/anno</strong> in licenze. The Custom plan (not Standard) is required for API access and multi-company — the Standard plan (~€22–28/utente/mese) lacks both.</li>
          <li><strong>Implementation cost (one-time):</strong> partner-led project required — Italian localization, data migration, training, and any custom modules: estimate <strong>€10,000–25,000</strong> depending on scope. Total Year 1: ~€12,000–27,500.</li>
          <li><strong>API:</strong> XML-RPC/JSON-RPC over the full ORM — most powerful data access available. Full trial balance, P&amp;L, all GL moves, per period — included in Custom plan at no extra cost.</li>
          <li><strong>Italian accounting compliance:</strong> <code>l10n_it_edi</code> — FatturaPA via SDI proxy K95IV18, withholding taxes, Ri.Ba., DDT, VAT export; liquidazioni IVA. Fiscal receipts (corrispettivi) are outside scope — TCA connects directly to Agenzia delle Entrate, no RT printer.</li>
          <li><strong>Regime 398/91 — not native:</strong> forfettario VAT, rendiconto format, and Modello EAS all require a custom partner-built module. Main barrier for an ASD/SSD without a dedicated IT budget.</li>
          <li><strong>Future scalability (hypothetical):</strong> if TCA ever needs HR, multi-company, multi-country, or additional modules on the same platform, Odoo can expand without a system migration — but this is outside the current accounting scope.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="fin-card fin-card--alt">
        <div class="fin-tag">Fallbacks</div>
        <div class="fin-title">TeamSystem Enterprise · Passepartout</div>
        <p class="fin-text"><strong>TSE in Cloud</strong> is a real candidate on paper (public developer portal with accounting movement services) but it is a full mid-market ERP — oversized for a club. <strong>Passepartout Passcom/Mexal</strong> is true accounting with a documented WebAPI, but journal-entry POST and balance GET would go through a partner-built PassBuilder/Sprix customization: feasible, with lock-in and custom development to budget.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fin-card fin-card--alt">
        <div class="fin-tag">Where Fatture in Cloud Still Fits</div>
        <div class="fin-title">Complementary Layer Only</div>
        <p class="fin-text">Best-documented API on the Italian market (OpenAPI spec, 8 SDKs, webhooks, API included in every paid plan) with native <code>payment_account</code>, revenue centers and SDI sending — but <strong>no chart of accounts, no double-entry, no balance endpoints</strong>. If the chosen GL system lacks a good SDI front-end, it could serve as the invoicing/receipts layer feeding the ledger; otherwise it drops out of the architecture.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── REGIME 398/91 ── -->
    <h2 class="aa-section-title">03 · Why Regime 398/91 <em>Changes Everything</em></h2>
    <div class="regime-alert">
      <div class="regime-alert-title">Critical question before choosing any software: is TCA an ASD or SSD operating under regime 398/91?</div>
      <p class="regime-alert-text">Virtually every Italian amateur sports club (circolo tennis included) qualifies for and uses <strong>Legge 398/1991</strong> if commercial revenues are below €400,000/year. This regime is not a minor tax detail — it changes the <em>entire accounting architecture</em> required.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="regime-grid">
      <div class="regime-card">
        <div class="regime-card-title">What regime 398/91 requires</div>
        <ul class="regime-list">
          <li><strong>Forfettario VAT:</strong> instead of collecting and remitting full VAT, the entity pays only 1/3 of the VAT shown on commercial invoices. Standard accounting software calculates full VAT — this mechanism must be built in or manually overridden.</li>
          <li><strong>Simplified bookkeeping:</strong> a <em>registro IVA minori</em> (simplified VAT register) is legally sufficient. Full double-entry is not mandatory — though it remains best practice for control.</li>
          <li><strong>Rendiconto economico-finanziario:</strong> the financial statement format is different from a standard Italian <em>bilancio d'esercizio</em> (OIC/IFRS). Most general-purpose accounting software produces the latter.</li>
          <li><strong>Institutional vs. commercial separation:</strong> revenues from institutional activities (membership fees, grants) are entirely outside IRES and VAT. This must be enforced at chart-of-accounts level.</li>
          <li><strong>Modello EAS:</strong> annual fiscal declaration for non-commercial entities (D.Lgs. 36/2021 Riforma dello Sport). No generic accounting software generates this.</li>
          <li><strong>Compensi sportivi dilettantistici:</strong> payments to athletes/coaches below €10,000 are IRPEF-exempt; the software must track individuals and thresholds.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="regime-card">
        <div class="regime-card-title">What each finalist handles</div>
        <ul class="regime-list">
          <li><strong>TeamSystem Sport:</strong> all of the above natively — purpose-built for this regime.</li>
          <li><strong>TeamSystem Contabilità in Cloud:</strong> handles double-entry accounting and Italian compliance; regime 398/91 requires configuration of the chart of accounts and manual processes for forfettario VAT — feasible but not automatic.</li>
          <li><strong>Odoo:</strong> none of the above natively. The forfettario VAT engine, rendiconto format, Modello EAS, and exempt-compensation tracking all require custom partner-built modules. This is a significant implementation cost on top of an already partner-heavy deployment.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="regime-card-title" style="margin-top:16px">Two architecture paths for TCA</div>
        <ul class="regime-list">
          <li><strong>Integrated path:</strong> TeamSystem Sport as the single system (club management + GL + regime 398/91 + SDI). Simpler, lower cost, less API flexibility.</li>
          <li><strong>Two-layer path:</strong> specialist club management system (Wansport, Golee, or TeamSystem Sport) for membership/courts/regime 398/91 + TeamSystem Contabilità in Cloud as the GL backend with full REST API for dashboards. More complex but gives the API power needed for Power BI / Looker Studio.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── PRICING COMPARISON ── -->
    <h2 class="aa-section-title">04 · Pricing <em>Comparison</em></h2>
    <p class="pricing-note">Figures below are indicative based on publicly available data (June 2026). Verify exact EUR amounts with each vendor before signing.</p>
